# SlideForge — local secrets. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this template is not, and must never carry a value.
# The server reads `.env` once at boot, so restart it after editing:
#
#   node server/server.js
#
# Real environment variables always win over this file, so a local .env can
# never override what Render's dashboard sets on the deployed app.

# Google AI Studio → Get API key → create a key for a project.
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# The whole value, no quotes, no spaces. Keys look like AQ.xxxxxxxx or AIza...
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Leave these alone unless you know you want different models.
#
# Moving aliases on purpose: keys issued in the newer AQ. format do not resolve
# pinned aliases such as gemini-2.5-flash, and the provider then answers 404
# for the MODEL — which reads as "model missing" when the key is perfectly
# good.
#
# Lite first on measurement: on a free-tier key, gemini-flash-latest answered
# 0 of 11 requests (nine fast 503s, two 30s hangs) while lite answered in
# 1-5 seconds. The server asks the fallback when the first is simply
# unavailable, so a bad afternoon for one alias is not a dead Write button.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest
GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACK=gemini-flash-latest
